    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight High Time and an inspired double rendition of Good Lovin'. Cryptical Envelopment segues flawlessly into Black Peter, highlighted by strong drums. Jerry's vocals are spot‑on and the mix captures Bob's guitar clearly.",
    "review": "On February 6, 1970 at the Fillmore West the Dead were in a fascinating early‑70 transitional phase, blending their country‑rock roots with lingering psychedelia. The soundboard recording (gd70-02-06.sbd.bean.3913.sbeok.shnf) offers a crisp, balanced mix that lets you hear Jerry singing his heart out and Bob’s guitar cutting through cleanly, even though six brief cuts interrupt the flow. Highlights include a soaring High Time, an energetic double Good Lovin' sandwich, and the seamless Cryptical Envelopment → Black Peter sequence where both Mickey and Billy lay down punchy drums. Despite the occasional “bricked” sections, the overall performance is solid, with Phil’s bass providing a sturdy foundation and the band moving as one through a two‑hour set that captures the era’s evolving sound.",
